@startuml seq_modify_booking
title Increment 6 - Modify Booking (FR-RS-05)
autonumber
hide footbox

actor Guest
actor Receptionist
boundary "Guest / Staff UI" as UI
control "Booking Management API" as API
control "Access Control" as Auth
control "Availability Service" as Avail
control "Billing / Simulated Payment" as Billing
database "Hotel Database" as DB

== Request and authorization ==
alt Guest modification
  Guest -> UI : Submit contact / guest count / date change
  UI -> API : Modify (reference, code, change, requestId)
  API -> Auth : Verify reference and code; rate-limit attempts
  Auth -> DB : Find reference and stored code hash
  DB --> Auth : Booking/hash or no match
  Auth -> Auth : Check code and per-booking scope
else Receptionist modification
  Receptionist -> UI : Submit change using staff account
  UI -> API : Modify (reservationId, staffSession, change, requestId)
  API -> Auth : Verify staff session and Receptionist role
end
Auth --> API : Authorized / denied

alt Unauthorized
  API --> UI : Deny without revealing booking details
else Authorized
  API -> DB : Read Confirmed status, original dates and version
  DB --> API : Current booking data
  alt Booking not Confirmed
    API --> UI : Reject; booking unchanged
  else Booking Confirmed
    API -> API : Validate fields, guest capacity and change policy
    opt Dates are changed
      API -> API : Require >= 24h before original 14:00 check-in
      API -> Avail : Precheck new nights (exclude current reservation)
      Avail --> API : Available / unavailable
    end
    alt Invalid input, late date change or no inventory
      API --> UI : Reject; original booking unchanged
    else Eligible change
      API -> Billing : Calculate revised JOD total and difference
      Billing --> API : Positive / zero / negative difference
      opt Positive difference
        API -> Billing : Attempt simulated additional payment (requestId)
        Billing --> API : Successful / failed
      end
      alt Required payment failed
        API --> UI : Reject; original booking unchanged
      else Payment not needed or successful
        API -> DB : BEGIN; lock booking and affected nightly inventory
        API -> DB : Recheck version, status, cutoff and capacity
        DB --> API : Eligible / conflict
        alt Conflict or changed eligibility
          API -> DB : ROLLBACK
          opt Additional payment already succeeded
            API -> Billing : Reverse or reconcile simulated charge
          end
          API --> UI : Reject; original booking unchanged
        else Eligible after recheck
          API -> DB : Commit updated details, dates/price snapshot,\ninventory difference and audit record
          DB --> API : Updated reservation saved
          opt Negative price difference
            API -> Billing : Refund simulated difference (requestId)
            Billing --> API : Refunded / needs reconciliation
          end
          API --> UI : Return updated booking (same reference and code)
        end
      end
    end
  end
end

note over API,DB
  A date change atomically releases old nights and consumes new nights.
  A failed change must preserve the original reservation.
  Payment/refund attempts use idempotency identifiers.
end note
@enduml
